BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 661.00 Tm (Quick warm-up, three questions - answer in your head, then we reveal.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 640.80 Tm (Question one: what does at-RequestBody do? Think... Reveal. It takes the JSON sent in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 625.60 Tm (request body and turns it into a Java object for you, automatically. You put it on a method) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 610.40 Tm (parameter, and Spring hands you a ready-filled object.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 590.20 Tm (Question two: what is the difference between POST and PUT? Think... Reveal. POST creates a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 575.00 Tm (brand-new thing - that is the C in CRUD. PUT updates something that already exists, usually found) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 559.80 Tm (by an id in the address - that is the U.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 539.60 Tm (And question three: what does at-PathVariable do? Reveal. It pulls a value straight out of the URL) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 524.40 Tm (path. In slash posts slash five, the 'five' gets handed to your method as the id.) Tj ET
