0.040 0.520 1.000 rg 58.00 653.60 496.00 1.40 re f
BT /F2 9.50 Tf 0.420 0.420 0.460 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 637.60 Tm (ON SCREEN) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 621.60 Tm (A definition and three reason cards: security, flexibility, decoupling.) Tj ET
0.720 0.720 0.760 rg 58.00 608.10 3.00 35.50 re f
BT /F2 9.50 Tf 0.040 0.340 0.780 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 597.60 Tm (SAY \(read this aloud\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 581.60 Tm (So, what is a DTO? It stands for Data Transfer Object, and it is exactly what the name says - a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 566.40 Tm (plain, simple Java class whose only job is to carry data between your app and the outside world. It) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 551.20 Tm (has no database annotations and no logic. It carries only what the caller actually needs. Let me) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 536.00 Tm (give you the three reasons we use one, shown as the three cards.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 515.80 Tm (First, security. You hide sensitive fields. The password lives on the entity, but it is simply not on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 500.60 Tm (DTO, so it can never slip out. We just saw that.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 480.40 Tm (Second, flexibility. You shape the response to fit the caller. Maybe one screen needs a short) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 465.20 Tm (summary and another needs full detail - you can have different DTOs for each, from the same) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 450.00 Tm (entity. You are not stuck sending every field every time.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 429.80 Tm (Third, decoupling - a fancy word for 'keeping things independent'. Your database can change) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 414.60 Tm (without breaking your public API. Rename a column, split a table - you just adjust the mapping) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 399.40 Tm (inside, and the callers outside never even notice.) Tj ET
0.040 0.520 1.000 rg 58.00 384.20 3.00 219.40 re f
BT /F2 9.50 Tf 0.040 0.340 0.780 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 375.40 Tm (EMPHASISE) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 359.40 Tm (Give them the one-liner to memorise: 'The entity maps to the database. The DTO travels over the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 344.20 Tm (wire.' They often look almost identical, but they exist for completely different reasons - and keeping) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 329.00 Tm (them separate is what lets an API grow safely over years.) Tj ET
0.040 0.520 1.000 rg 58.00 313.80 3.00 67.60 re f
