BT /F1 10.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 233.50 Tm (responsibility.) Tj ET
0.720 0.720 0.760 rg 58.00 220.00 3.00 49.00 re f
BT /F2 9.50 Tf 0.040 0.340 0.780 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 209.50 Tm (SAY \(read this aloud\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 193.50 Tm (This slide is the backbone of the whole session, so let's go slowly. A professional Spring Boot app) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 178.30 Tm (is split into layers, and each layer has exactly one job. A request flows down through them, and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 163.10 Tm (response flows back up. Let me walk you down the pipeline.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 142.90 Tm (The Client - a browser, a phone, a testing tool - sends an HTTP request. It arrives at the Controller,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 127.70 Tm (marked at-RestController. The controller's only job is to deal with the web - take the request, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 112.50 Tm (pass a DTO down to the service. Then the Service, marked at-Service, holds the business logic -) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 97.30 Tm (the actual thinking - and it does the mapping between DTO and entity. The service calls the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 82.10 Tm (Repository, marked at-Repository, whose only job is talking to the database using the entity. And) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 66.90 Tm (finally the Database stores and retrieves the real data.) Tj ET
