BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 750.00 Tm (you a post or crash. Instead it hands you an Optional - which is like a little box that might contain a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 734.80 Tm (post, or might be empty. It is Java's polite way of saying 'maybe it is here, maybe it is not - you) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 719.60 Tm (must handle both'.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 699.40 Tm (And handling both is easy with one method - orElseThrow. Follow the two paths on screen.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 684.20 Tm (findById gives you the box. If the post is inside, orElseThrow opens the box and hands it to you. If) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 669.00 Tm (the box is empty, orElseThrow throws your ResourceNotFoundException - which becomes the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 653.80 Tm (clean 404. Read the code out loud and it almost makes sense in plain English: 'find by id, or else) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 638.60 Tm (throw this exception'.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 618.40 Tm (So with one line, you handle the happy case and the missing case, no messy null checks needed.) Tj ET
0.040 0.520 1.000 rg 58.00 603.20 3.00 162.00 re f
BT /F2 9.50 Tf 0.040 0.340 0.780 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 594.40 Tm (EMPHASISE) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 578.40 Tm (Warn about the common mistake in the red box: never call dot get on an Optional directly. If the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 563.20 Tm (box is empty, dot get throws a generic, unhelpful error with no message. Always use orElseThrow,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 548.00 Tm (so YOU control both the exception and the friendly message the caller sees.) Tj ET
