0.040 0.520 1.000 rg 58.00 344.90 496.00 1.40 re f
BT /F2 9.50 Tf 0.420 0.420 0.460 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 328.90 Tm (ON SCREEN) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 312.90 Tm (A load-balancer diagram: clients to a load balancer to three instances of a service.) Tj ET
0.720 0.720 0.760 rg 58.00 299.40 3.00 35.50 re f
BT /F2 9.50 Tf 0.040 0.340 0.780 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 288.90 Tm (SAY \(read this aloud\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 272.90 Tm (So if you have three copies of a service running, a natural question pops up - which copy does) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 257.70 Tm (each request go to? That is the job of a load balancer. It sits in front of your copies and spreads the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 242.50 Tm (incoming traffic evenly across them. Think of it as the person at the front of a bank who directs you) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 227.30 Tm (to whichever teller is free.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 207.10 Tm (This gives us two big wins. First, load balancing itself - no single copy gets overwhelmed, because) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 191.90 Tm (the work is shared. And second, high availability - this is the important one. If one copy crashes,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 176.70 Tm (the load balancer simply notices and stops sending traffic to it. The other copies keep serving, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 161.50 Tm (your users never even notice there was a problem. The system stays up.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 141.30 Tm (In the Spring world, this is handled by tools in Spring Cloud - things with names like Eureka and an) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 126.10 Tm (API Gateway. Don't worry about those names yet - they are exactly what we build, hands-on, in) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 110.90 Tm (Session 4. For now, just hold the picture: a traffic director sharing work across copies, keeping) Tj ET
BT /F1 11.00 Tf 0.120 0.120 0.140 rg 1 0 0 1 72.00 95.70 Tm (everything running smoothly.) Tj ET
